on the broadcast.

01:03:34.644 --> 01:03:37.524
Eunho: Wow, that was a very long preparation period.

01:03:37.564 --> 01:03:39.964
Hamin: Yes, this took about six rehearsals.
Yejun: About six times. Around six times. Yeah.

01:03:40.004 --> 01:03:41.744
Hamin: The lines sounded pretty natural.

01:03:41.784 --> 01:03:42.884
Hamin: I used that higher placement.
Eunho: Oh... Good. Clear. Definitely.

01:03:42.924 --> 01:03:44.747
Yejun: It was good. I liked it.

01:03:45.704 --> 01:03:48.084
Eunho: Yes... Great. Shall we move on to the next one?

01:03:48.124 --> 01:03:50.604
Hamin: Great. ja, let's skip ahead to the next question.

01:03:50.644 --> 01:03:52.055
Yejun: What, what, what?

01:03:52.884 --> 01:03:57.792
Hamin: 'While preparing the stage, did anyone secretly practice a
signature expression...

01:03:57.832 --> 01:04:02.004
Hamin: ...or a special gesture or choreography point?'

01:04:02.164 --> 01:04:06.752
Hamin: That's the question. ja, has anyone ever practiced something in
secret?

01:04:08.244 --> 01:04:11.420
Noah: I didn't exactly practice in secret. Honestly...

01:04:11.504 --> 01:04:13.764
Noah: I did it openly. Anyone secretly practiced?
Hamin: Keep practicing.

01:04:13.804 --> 01:04:15.544
Yejun: Same here. Actually, I did.
Hamin: Not secretly, more like personal research.

01:04:15.584 --> 01:04:17.936
Bamby: What do you mean by "originally"?

01:04:18.284 --> 01:04:18.924
Yejun: Hey. I was just practicing a little gesture on my own.

01:04:18.964 --> 01:04:23.744
Hamin: You know, stuff like that—your own part, or maybe right now,
like, should we add something here?

01:04:23.784 --> 01:04:25.506
Eunho: Oh... I guess you could call it practice?
Hamin: Maybe try adding anything at all?

01:04:25.546 --> 01:04:28.124
Eunho: I've actually thought about this before—back at home.

01:04:28.164 --> 01:04:34.431
Eunho: At home, I thought about the 'boom!' at the end of our stage.
There's choreography that matches that moment.

01:04:34.471 --> 01:04:38.204
Eunho: After the dance break, there are two beats, then it whooshes
past.

01:04:38.244 --> 01:04:39.644
Hamin: Ah, here

01:04:40.004 --> 01:04:45.309
Eunho: At that moment, I did a lot of gestures all by myself... Let me
try this, I've tried this before—like this...

01:04:45.349 --> 01:04:49.804
Eunho: when it goes "dong-dong," something like... dong! dong! There's
also this...

01:04:49.844 --> 01:04:52.524
Bamby: What? Just now.
Eunho: This is a bit...

01:04:52.564 --> 01:04:55.604
Eunho: It's going so fast that it feels like I'm being blown away by
the wind.

01:04:55.644 --> 01:04:57.004
Hamin: Uh oh, flying away
Eunho: Two! Two!

01:04:57.044 --> 01:04:58.808
Hamin: Uh, this... who's this?

01:04:59.104 --> 01:05:01.444
Hamin: It feels like I'm pulling it off like this, puffy and all?

01:05:01.484 --> 01:05:04.364
Eunho: But... But it took up too much space, so I dropped the idea.

01:05:04.404 --> 01:05:06.951
Bamby: Ah, right. Right. The range... The movement has a lot of depth,
yes.

01:05:06.991 --> 01:05:12.124
Eunho: Stuff like that happened. I didn't mention it before, but this
is the first time I'm bringing it up now.

01:05:12.164 --> 01:05:15.164
Bamby: Good call. You did well not to say anything.

01:05:19.104 --> 01:05:22.204
Bamby: It was best that you only thought about it. [Laughs]

01:05:22.244 --> 01:05:27.266
Hamin: Great. The composer line practiced openly, and from what I've
seen...

01:05:27.306 --> 01:05:32.244
Hamin: ...BAMBY is well known among us for changing gestures like
these.

01:05:33.644 --> 01:05:39.055
Yejun: He's definitely known for it.
Hamin: At the beginning, there's that 'ing-ing' part...

01:05:39.524 --> 01:05:41.004
Bamby: Ah, don't make that sound like that.

01:05:41.044 --> 01:05:44.764
Hamin: Ah, I'm sorry, I'm sorry. No, it's just, since it's a
broadcast, I was trying to be funny.

01:05:44.804 --> 01:05:45.584
Bamby: Okay. Good. Yeah.

01:05:45.624 --> 01:05:50.179
Hamin: I was only making it sound funny for the broadcast. I think I
made this part...

01:05:50.219 --> 01:05:51.944
Hamin: but where exactly is it—somewhere in the chorus section?

01:05:51.984 --> 01:05:55.384
Eunho: Making the sound funny...
Hamin: This one before

01:05:57.024 --> 01:05:58.064
Hamin: What is this part?
Bamby: What was this part again?

01:05:58.104 --> 01:05:59.444
Hamin: Oh, bang bang—this is it, isn't it?
Noah: [Imitates the beat]

01:05:59.484 --> 01:06:00.404
Bamby: Originally, they were all the same. All five of them.

01:06:00.444 --> 01:06:08.284
Hamin: Right. I originally made it the same for all five members, but
BAMBY suddenly added a spin and hit this pose.

01:06:10.364 --> 01:06:12.004
Bamby: Um... If it's gestures, then it's gestures. I mean, I did it
again...

01:06:12.044 --> 01:06:13.904
Yejun: Maybe it's just gestures.

01:06:13.944 --> 01:06:15.324
Bamby: Why? Mmm, because.

01:06:15.364 --> 01:06:19.344
Bamby: When it's in the center, there's this feeling that you have to
do something a little special...

01:06:19.384 --> 01:06:21.684
Bamby: ...so I felt I should do something special. And this move...

01:06:21.724 --> 01:06:22.684
Hamin: It felt really drift-like from my perspective.

01:06:22.724 --> 01:06:26.524
Bamby: It felt kinda drift-like, like all five of us doing it the same
way...

01:06:26.564 --> 01:06:30.004
Bamby: ...doing it was cool, but we did it that way at first, didn't
we.

01:06:30.044 --> 01:06:31.444
Bamby: What's so funny?

01:06:32.324 --> 01:06:34.184
Hamin: Why are you suddenly explaining it so seriously?

01:06:34.224 --> 01:06:35.354
Eunho: Ohhh! Hey! Ohhh! Me!
Noah: [Imitates the beat]

01:06:35.394 --> 01:06:37.824
Hamin: Come to the middle and say it properly.

01:06:37.864 --> 01:06:40.624
Eunho: Ohhh! Being grumpy today?
Yejun: Ah. Teams are different. Our team is different.

01:06:40.664 --> 01:06:46.075
Hamin: Yes, this is Ataji's team.
Yejun: Yes. Teams are different. Teams are different. Yes.

01:06:47.024 --> 01:06:48.424
Eunho: This is funny!

01:06:49.304 --> 01:06:51.284
Hamin: ja, anyway...
Noah: Okay, okay, so anyway,

01:06:51.324 --> 01:06:53.484
Hamin: BAMBY added a flashier performance element.

01:06:53.524 --> 01:06:58.641
Bamby: That's right. That's right. It felt a bit... kind of bland, so
at first we practiced that way...

01:06:58.681 --> 01:07:03.151
Bamby: Actually, I changed it only two or three days before the first
shoot.

01:07:08.244 --> 01:07:10.655
Eunho: How about showing us?
Bamby: No...

01:07:12.484 --> 01:07:15.344
Eunho: No, I'm on the same team, so I get a chance... I'm on your
team, so...

01:07:15.384 --> 01:07:17.164
Hamin: Oh, this part here, the part where you turn back like this

01:07:17.204 --> 01:07:20.204
Eunho: No, show me once.
Hamin: This part looks cool, but I just can't keep up.

01:07:20.244 --> 01:07:22.164
Eunho: No, because I'm on the same team...

01:07:22.204 --> 01:07:22.964
Hamin: Right here
Bamby: What was it again? The choreography...

01:07:23.004 --> 01:07:25.104
Hamin: From the ground, ground, ground...
Bamby: Ditto, ditto, ditto... Oh! Ah!

01:07:25.144 --> 01:07:28.924
Noah: [Imitates the beat]

01:07:28.964 --> 01:07:30.364
Hamin: Ground

01:07:31.344 --> 01:07:35.680
Eunho: No, and BAMBY, the one I found—there are more, one by one.

01:07:35.720 --> 01:07:42.318
Eunho: It's like he's doing this solo thing, nodding his head like
this. Ah! That's the point move! Kind of like,

01:07:42.358 --> 01:07:46.164
Eunho: there's this moment where it feels a bit like I'm solo center
here?

01:07:46.204 --> 01:07:47.884
Bamby: Be specific, please.
Eunho: No, no, in the chorus of verse 2.

01:07:47.924 --> 01:07:49.984
Noah: Wait a second—did BAMBY ever do that kind of choreography in the
center?

01:07:50.024 --> 01:07:51.864
Eunho: How did they do the chorus of verse 2?
Bamby: This one? Ahhh, finally this one?

01:07:51.904 --> 01:07:54.804
Hamin: This, this—ah, this is what they do

01:07:55.244 --> 01:07:56.044
Bamby: This one?
Eunho: E! That's it, that's it!

01:07:56.084 --> 01:07:58.084
Hamin: Ah, this, this.
Eunho: That's it!

01:07:58.124 --> 01:08:00.829
Bamby: What is this?
Eunho: Is that a gesture?

01:08:01.164 --> 01:08:04.744
Bamby: Ah, I don't know. It's probably a dance or a gesture, right?
Hamin: This one is

01:08:04.784 --> 01:08:05.984
Eunho: Got it.
Bamby: It's probably one of the two, you know.

01:08:06.024 --> 01:08:07.004
Eunho: Understood.

01:08:07.044 --> 01:08:12.164
Hamin: No, this was clearly taken from the choreographers' original
draft.

01:08:12.364 --> 01:08:13.964
Bamby: This? I made this from scratch.

01:08:14.004 --> 01:08:16.164
Hamin: This one? This one?
Bamby: This is mine.

01:08:16.204 --> 01:08:17.484
Eunho: Oh, really?
Hamin: But I saw that in the original draft.

01:08:17.524 --> 01:08:19.229
Bamby: It wasn't there, this.

01:08:19.584 --> 01:08:24.878
Hamin: Hyung said, ‘Let's use this one from the draft.’
Bamby: No. This isn't here, is it?

01:08:25.684 --> 01:08:28.044
Bamby: Put this in.
Hamin: Oh, not this one, this one, not this one

01:08:28.084 --> 01:08:28.944
Hamin: It's here, it's here, huh?

01:08:28.984 --> 01:08:32.984
Bamby: It was already there? I didn't know—I thought I'd made it up.

01:08:33.744 --> 01:08:35.464
Eunho: No way, you're shameless!
Noah: Ugh, seriously, why is he like that?

01:08:35.504 --> 01:08:37.324
Eunho: No way, you're shameless! Seriously!
Bamby: No...

01:08:37.364 --> 01:08:39.305
Bamby: If that's true, I'm sorry.

01:08:40.764 --> 01:08:42.344
Hamin: He says he's sorry.

01:08:42.384 --> 01:08:44.584
Bamby: Oh, I'm sorry.
Eunho: No way, totally shameless!

01:08:44.624 --> 01:08:45.544
Yejun: Ah. So that's what I mean. Ah.
Eunho: Hohoho! Hoho!

01:08:45.584 --> 01:08:47.644
Bamby: My head is all mixed up right now.

01:08:47.684 --> 01:08:50.984
Hamin: Of course anyone could get confused.
Bamby: I genuinely thought I'd created it.

01:08:51.024 --> 01:08:53.906
Yejun: Of course, that can happen. It can happen.

01:08:56.024 --> 01:08:57.969
Hamin: Anyway, it became a really cool piece of choreography.

01:08:58.009 --> 01:09:03.424
Hamin: BAMBY is always studying and revising gestures like that, and I
tend to do the same—adding variations.

01:09:03.464 --> 01:09:07.404
Eunho: But you told me I did well by only thinking about mine. I
understand. Let's move on.

01:09:07.444 --> 01:09:13.224
Hamin: ja, that answers that question. ja, next... Next: 'The Answer
Is Yes'—the group-chant recording...

01:09:13.264 --> 01:09:15.084
Bamby: Tell us the story!

01:09:16.684 --> 01:09:18.544
Eunho: Oh, this was fun, right?
Yejun: It was really fun.

01:09:18.584 --> 01:09:23.724
Hamin: 'Did you all enter the studio together and record several
versions? We'd love to hear the recording stories.'

01:09:23.764 --> 01:09:26.604
Noah: Uh, of course.
Hamin: ja, tell us about the recording session.

01:09:26.644 --> 01:09:28.684
Eunho: We really did it in many different versions.

01:09:28.724 --> 01:09:34.664
Yejun: Yes. We had so much fun. Honestly, it felt like we were just
laughing uncontrollably while doing it.

01:09:34.704 --> 01:09:38.444
Yejun: I already brought my MacBook along, actually.

01:09:38.964 --> 01:09:39.824
Noah: Ah, the recorded version?

01:09:39.864 --> 01:09:41.804
Yejun: How about we open the project and listen to them one by one?
Hamin: ja, is there a file for this now?

01:09:41.844 --> 01:09:44.604
Bamby: Wow, you actually brought it.

01:09:45.904 --> 01:09:52.104
Yejun: When PLLI hear the polished, mastered version, it all sounds
great,

01:09:52.144 --> 01:09:53.544
Bamby: Oh my, oh my.

01:09:55.344 --> 01:09:59.108
Yejun: but when we peel back the individual tracks one by one...

01:09:59.344 --> 01:10:02.544
Noah: Why, why, why, why?
Yejun: Huh? Ahhh. Huh?

01:10:11.644 --> 01:10:15.344
Yejun: I organized the vocal tracks and brought them along today.

01:10:15.384 --> 01:10:20.736
Bamby: Is there more of this too?
Yejun: Give me a moment—I have everything organized here.

01:10:21.904 --> 01:10:24.764
Yejun: You know the part that goes 'na, na, na'?

01:10:24.944 --> 01:10:27.624
Yejun: That part ended up having a whopping 37 tracks.

01:10:27.664 --> 01:10:29.064
Noah: Thirty-seven?

01:10:29.904 --> 01:10:33.264
Yejun: Thirty-seven tracks: five in the center...

01:10:33.804 --> 01:10:37.384
Yejun: ...and another 32 spread across the sides. That's how much we
recorded.

01:10:37.424 --> 01:10:42.824
Noah: Just for the bridge? We recorded that much?
Yejun: Yes. The group-chant section has 37 tracks.

01:10:42.864 --> 01:10:45.452
Yejun: ja, shall we listen to one at a time?

01:10:48.664 --> 01:10:51.604
Noah: Oh, you mean 37 when all the different sections are combined,
right?

01:10:51.644 --> 01:10:53.384
Yejun: What do you mean?
Noah: It's not just the bridge, though.

01:10:53.424 --> 01:10:54.924
Yejun: Bridge one.
Noah: Just the bridge being 37?

01:10:54.964 --> 01:10:57.684
Yejun: Bridge one alone has 37 tracks.
Noah: We recorded 37 tracks just for the bridge?

01:10:57.724 --> 01:11:00.044
Bamby: Of course, hyung—just for this part.

01:11:00.084 --> 01:11:01.484
Noah: Oh, really?

01:11:02.104 --> 01:11:03.692
Bamby: We really did a lot.

01:11:05.524 --> 01:11:07.524
Yejun: Shall we listen one by one?

01:11:09.624 --> 01:11:13.094
Noah: So that's what we did for this bridge. Ahhh, ahhhh...

01:11:15.004 --> 01:11:18.239
Yejun: Give me a moment. Let's hear which part this is.

01:11:19.164 --> 01:11:20.564
Yejun: Can't hear it?

01:11:22.064 --> 01:11:25.181
Yejun: We can't hear it right now. What should we do?

01:11:27.224 --> 01:11:29.282
Hamin: So it says we're connecting.

01:11:29.944 --> 01:11:33.744
Yejun: Ah, this is 'The Answer Is Yes.' Let's listen to the tracks one
by one.

01:11:33.784 --> 01:11:36.364
Yejun: First, in 'The Answer Is Yes'...

01:11:38.964 --> 01:11:41.044
Hamin: Oh, a clean, straightforward take.

01:11:41.084 --> 01:11:42.613
Yejun: What could this be?

01:11:43.724 --> 01:11:47.524
Yejun: That's one group-chant layer.
Hamin: A slightly more energetic version.

01:11:47.564 --> 01:11:50.505
Yejun: There's one more. What else could there be?

01:11:52.304 --> 01:11:56.715
Yejun: We recorded another layer to give it a little more weight and
punch.

01:11:58.164 --> 01:11:59.564
Yejun: Next.

01:12:00.724 --> 01:12:02.124
Hamin: Low version

01:12:03.804 --> 01:12:07.664
Yejun: We recorded that one in a lower register. Next...

01:12:09.044 --> 01:12:12.396
Yejun: This is the military-style delivery we're good at.

01:12:13.104 --> 01:12:14.764
Yejun: We tried it with that kind of feel.

01:12:14.804 --> 01:12:17.568
Yejun: And lastly, a nasal, buzzy kind of take.

01:12:18.044 --> 01:12:19.455
Hamin: Ah, a thin voice.

01:12:20.604 --> 01:12:22.824
Bamby: Why does EUNHO's voice come through so clearly?

01:12:22.864 --> 01:12:25.984
Bamby: Is it just me?
Eunho: Oh, my voice is really loud.

01:12:26.024 --> 01:12:28.228
Eunho: When Noah-hyung gives me a guide, he's always saying...

01:12:28.268 --> 01:12:34.185
Eunho: 'Wait, sorry—let's do that again. It peaked.' Every time. So he
always turns my volume down...

01:12:34.225 --> 01:12:37.604
Eunho: And I'm always saying, 'Hyung, I think I messed up.'

01:12:37.644 --> 01:12:41.224
Noah: Whenever EUNHO uses the guide mic, I tell him to sing with it
this far away.

01:12:41.264 --> 01:12:43.205
Noah: His voice is that powerful.

01:12:47.004 --> 01:12:49.844
Yejun: When we combine them...

01:12:50.384 --> 01:12:53.484
Yejun: ...we get this great group chant. Now let's hear the next
layers one by one.

01:12:53.524 --> 01:12:55.994
Yejun: Shall we start listening from here?

01:12:56.164 --> 01:12:57.564
Eunho: This is fun.

01:13:01.204 --> 01:13:04.145
Bamby: Wow, why does my voice sound so clear here?

01:13:05.844 --> 01:13:08.804
Eunho: Bamby-hyung, Noah-hyung, you both sound really clear.
Bamby: You're right.

01:13:08.844 --> 01:13:12.667
Bamby: I think my voice sounds very similar to Noah-hyung's here.

01:13:16.764 --> 01:13:20.444
Yejun: This is the low-register layer.

01:13:23.184 --> 01:13:24.824
Yejun: Let's go up a bit.

01:13:32.084 --> 01:13:34.025
Yejun: And there's one more next.

01:13:36.524 --> 01:13:38.465
Yejun: A bit more powerful voice.

01:13:43.504 --> 01:13:47.504
Eunho: We sing this slightly off the beat—that gives it more flavor.

01:13:51.004 --> 01:13:54.804
Yejun: And now, we're starting to add a bit more flavor.

01:13:55.284 --> 01:14:00.636
Noah: Getting everyone lined up was really funny.
Eunho: [Demonstrates another vocal layer]

01:14:03.244 --> 01:14:05.684
Yejun: We kept adding sounds like that.

01:14:07.877 --> 01:14:13.347
Yejun: I listened to all of these one by one earlier. There are really
a lot of angry people.

01:14:17.104 --> 01:14:19.184
Yejun: So far, it's still mild.

01:14:24.504 --> 01:14:28.856
Yejun: ja, up to this point, we stacked the voices the way we normally
do.

01:14:29.004 --> 01:14:32.415
Yejun: From here on, quite a few of the takes sound angry.

01:14:34.644 --> 01:14:36.879
Noah: No, we had to commit to it here.

01:14:37.964 --> 01:14:40.493
Bamby: Not exactly angry—more like wailing.

01:14:41.684 --> 01:14:44.964
Eunho: Noah-hyung is really good at this...
Noah: Wait, isn't that my voice?

01:14:45.004 --> 01:14:46.064
Yejun: Just a sec. Let me listen to it one more time.

01:14:46.104 --> 01:14:50.280
Hamin: Anyone can tell that's you, hyung—all we can hear is your
voice.

01:14:54.244 --> 01:14:57.964
Eunho: That's Noah-hyung, isn't it?
Yejun: Was that tough, members?

01:14:58.004 --> 01:15:03.592
Noah: But at the time...the direction from the start was to wail with
a slightly pathetic edge.

01:15:06.844 --> 01:15:09.544
Yejun: And one more thing.

01:15:09.584 --> 01:15:11.878
Eunho: Wow, this. It's not easy, is it?

01:15:17.724 --> 01:15:21.964
Bamby: That's NOAH. Hyung, this is your solo track—your solo track.
Hamin: I don't think we should reveal whose take this is.

01:15:22.004 --> 01:15:24.844
Noah: Let me say one thing: BAMBY's voice...

01:15:28.104 --> 01:15:30.164
Noah: ...is fairly similar to mine.

01:15:32.664 --> 01:15:34.644
Yejun: In the higher register.

01:15:36.724 --> 01:15:38.624
Noah: PLLI have said they sometimes mix our voices up too.

01:15:38.664 --> 01:15:43.336
Noah: When I said I wanted this to sound like a wail...BAMBY
understood and expressed it the best.

01:15:43.376 --> 01:15:48.024
Noah: I could tell from right beside him. He really wailed right
beside me.

01:15:48.464 --> 01:15:51.364
Eunho: But I... I saw Bamby-hyung's expression, and it really shocked
me.

01:15:51.404 --> 01:15:53.604
Bamby: Oh, really?
Noah: Bamby, you know the expression I mean, right?

01:15:53.644 --> 01:15:57.879
Noah: I told him, 'Make this expression.'
Eunho: I'll... show you first.

01:15:58.184 --> 01:16:02.184
Noah: Yes, that's exactly how he did it.

01:16:02.224 --> 01:16:03.584
Eunho: I was really startled.
Yejun: That really startled me too.

01:16:03.624 --> 01:16:05.584
Noah: Listening from behind, I thought, 'Wow, he must have a lot pent
up.'

01:16:05.624 --> 01:16:07.024
Hamin: He nailed it.

01:16:07.344 --> 01:16:08.825
Noah: Bamby really sounded like he was wailing.

01:16:08.865 --> 01:16:12.484
Eunho: I thought this was a music video shoot location, not a
recording studio.

01:16:12.524 --> 01:16:15.284
Eunho: You were acting so intensely with your face...
Bamby: Of course. It's method acting.

01:16:15.324 --> 01:16:18.853
Yejun: ja, that's the version where we added more character.

01:16:20.024 --> 01:16:22.224
Yejun: We stacked all of those layers together.

01:16:22.264 --> 01:16:24.424
Noah: At the end, when we finally let it go, it's seriously amazing.

01:16:24.464 --> 01:16:26.544
Noah: That part, that part — we really nailed the acting, we all did
great.

01:16:26.584 --> 01:16:30.124
Yejun: Shall we listen to the layers at the end too? Keep it playing.
Eunho: This part is really... wow...

01:16:30.164 --> 01:16:33.784
Yejun: This one goes without saying.
Noah: This is one of the mild takes.

01:16:33.824 --> 01:16:39.244
Bamby: This one is basically an EUNHO solo.
Yejun: A lot of us are in this one. ja, second one coming up.

01:16:39.284 --> 01:16:41.284
Yejun: This one's supposed to be stacked too.

01:16:41.324 --> 01:16:42.912
Yejun: Third one coming up.

01:16:55.664 --> 01:16:58.487
Yejun: Oh, listening in.
Noah: Let's keep going.

01:16:59.924 --> 01:17:01.964
Noah: This is the standard bright high-register layer.
Eunho: Hey, what are you talking about?

01:17:02.004 --> 01:17:03.404
Yejun: ja, next...

01:17:04.504 --> 01:17:06.304
Hamin: Ah, it's starting to change a little by little now

01:17:06.344 --> 01:17:12.049
Noah: [Laughs] This one sits right here.
Yejun: Someone starts laughing in the background—listen.

01:17:12.544 --> 01:17:14.564
Bamby: Me. This is me. Remember?
Yejun: ja, we used a layer like that too.

01:17:14.604 --> 01:17:16.004
Yejun: And finally...

01:17:18.424 --> 01:17:21.324
Yejun: ja, that completes the stack.

01:17:26.784 --> 01:17:28.184
Bamby: Wait—what?

01:17:28.544 --> 01:17:33.896
Hamin: 'HYPERDRIVE,' the fifth mini album...has reached a new career
high. Congratulations!

01:17:36.244 --> 01:17:37.644
Yejun: Really?

01:17:45.324 --> 01:17:47.676
Yejun: Wow, really?
Noah: What do we do?

01:17:49.324 --> 01:17:52.794
Noah: Really?
Eunho: I guess I have to dance one more time.

01:17:53.124 --> 01:17:56.364
Eunho: Wow, this is really amazing.
Noah: I just got goosebumps. Is that really true?

01:17:56.404 --> 01:17:58.484
Hamin: I've got goosebumps all over.

01:17:58.524 --> 01:18:03.700
Bamby: So this really can happen.
Hamin: PLLI prepared this wonderful surprise for us...

01:18:04.904 --> 01:18:06.284
Eunho: Wow, this is really amazing.

01:18:06.324 --> 01:18:10.704
Hamin: Thank you so much for this wonderful gift and for celebrating
with us.

01:18:10.744 --> 01:18:16.744
Hamin: We'll work even harder and become responsible artists...so
PLAVE can keep going from strength to strength.

01:18:17.904 --> 01:18:19.664
Eunho: Wow, really... No...

01:18:22.124 --> 01:18:24.535
Eunho: Ah... I can't even find the words.

01:18:25.724 --> 01:18:28.144
Hamin: NOAH-ssi, it looks like you've got serious goosebumps.

01:18:28.184 --> 01:18:31.125
Noah: I really do have goosebumps. I'm not joking.

01:18:31.344 --> 01:18:34.284
Noah: Oh, I'm cold!
Hamin: 'I'm cold,' he says! Tell us how you feel.

01:18:34.324 --> 01:18:37.912
Hamin: How can you even express this exact feeling right now?

01:18:38.904 --> 01:18:42.224
Noah: Honestly, I wasn't expecting this at all.

01:18:43.544 --> 01:18:50.224
Noah: Really—because our previous results were already so high...that
I couldn't imagine going even higher.

01:18:51.184 --> 01:18:54.244
Eunho: I can't help but think about how we started.

01:18:58.064 --> 01:18:59.464
Eunho: This is amazing.

01:19:01.204 --> 01:19:03.792
Hamin: I'm feeling so many emotions at once.

01:19:10.084 --> 01:19:12.658
Eunho: We talked about this at the very beginning, remember?

01:19:12.698 --> 01:19:17.874
Eunho: When we heard they were printing 5,000 albums, we
wondered...'Will that be okay?'

01:19:20.904 --> 01:19:26.664
Eunho: But thanks to all the love from PLLI...we've been able to grow
steadily and come this far.

01:19:27.364 --> 01:19:30.422
Eunho: Wow... now a day like this has actually come.

01:19:33.424 --> 01:19:35.584
Yejun: Wow, thank you so much. Truly.

01:19:35.624 --> 01:19:43.464
Eunho: This career high is truly...entirely thanks to PLLI. You made
all of this possible...

01:19:43.884 --> 01:19:46.984
Eunho: ...and the result feels like a miracle.

01:19:49.084 --> 01:19:55.644
Hamin: And I'm so glad we reached this career high live...while we
could see each other's faces.

01:19:57.044 --> 01:20:02.985
Hamin: I wish I could express this feeling beautifully and share it
with you in every possible way...

01:20:04.704 --> 01:20:09.056
Hamin: ...but as you can see, all of us are at a loss for words right
now.

01:20:09.884 --> 01:20:13.884
Hamin: I feel so happy and so deeply loved.

01:20:14.884 --> 01:20:16.544
Hamin: I'm truly overwhelmed.

01:20:16.584 --> 01:20:20.764
Eunho: Whenever I feel like this, there's something I always say to
PLLI...

01:20:20.804 --> 01:20:25.862
Eunho: What kind of life are we living, to be blessed with so much to
be grateful for?

01:20:30.664 --> 01:20:32.284
Eunho: What do we do, leader...?
Hamin: Please say a few words.

01:20:32.324 --> 01:20:34.364
Eunho: Yejun-hyung.
Yejun: First,

01:20:34.404 --> 01:20:36.304
Eunho: We'd appreciate your thoughts.

01:20:36.344 --> 01:20:41.944
Yejun: First, I really want to say how grateful I am. To all of you,
PLLI.

01:20:42.284 --> 01:20:44.944
Yejun: PLLI made all of this happen for us.

01:20:45.644 --> 01:20:48.124
Yejun: Honestly, with this album...

01:20:54.904 --> 01:20:58.433
Yejun: I honestly never focused on things like career highs.

01:20:58.904 --> 01:21:01.904
Yejun: I was simply so happy to release this album.

01:21:04.024 --> 01:21:07.494
Yejun: I was happy from the very beginning, because PLLI...

01:21:10.604 --> 01:21:14.368
Yejun: ...were excited about this album even before it came out.

01:21:16.084 --> 01:21:19.999
Yejun: You were saying, 'PLAVE are promoting again, and this concept
is amazing!'

01:21:20.039 --> 01:21:23.921
Yejun: And PLLI rallied together, saying, 'Let's give it our all.'

01:21:27.924 --> 01:21:30.584
Yejun: That alone made me so happy.

01:21:31.864 --> 01:21:37.244
Yejun: A career high means setting a new record for ourselves.

01:21:38.544 --> 01:21:40.424
Yejun: And that's incredibly difficult.

01:21:40.464 --> 01:21:45.424
Yejun: Our previous results were already so good, so...

01:21:45.944 --> 01:21:50.296
Yejun: ...just seeing PLLI enjoy something they love makes me truly
happy.

01:21:52.344 --> 01:21:57.285
Yejun: Since PLLI loved it so much, we said we'd be happy just
releasing this album.

01:22:05.884 --> 01:22:10.119
Yejun: And now PLLI have given us this enormous gift. Thank you so
much.

01:22:12.004 --> 01:22:14.651
Hamin: ja, members, let's all hug each other.

01:22:15.364 --> 01:22:17.184
Hamin: You all worked hard.

01:22:19.664 --> 01:22:21.840
Eunho: You all worked hard. Really...

01:22:22.964 --> 01:22:28.644
Eunho: PLLI, seriously, you've worked so hard. Come here.
Yejun: PLLI, you've worked so hard. Thank you so much.

01:22:28.684 --> 01:22:33.204
Yejun: PLLI, we know how incredibly hard you've worked.

01:22:37.804 --> 01:22:43.804
Yejun: We talk about this all the time—on our way to work, over meals
before concerts, or during breaks.

01:22:48.126 --> 01:22:53.184
Yejun: We often say how hard PLLI have been working lately, especially
for this album.

01:22:54.904 --> 01:22:57.021
Yejun: We know how much you've done.

01:23:02.104 --> 01:23:06.692
Yejun: I'm so happy about this career high, but I also feel sorry
toward PLLI.

01:23:11.224 --> 01:23:16.812
Noah: When we were working and practicing, we knew our previous
results were already very high.

01:23:21.844 --> 01:23:27.844
Noah: So this time, instead of thinking about results, we focused on
showing you even better quality and music.

01:23:30.004 --> 01:23:33.827
Noah: We prepared it because we wanted to give PLLI many gifts...

01:23:35.884 --> 01:23:39.178
Noah: ...but here we are receiving another gift instead.

01:23:41.544 --> 01:23:43.924
Noah: Thank you so much. Truly.

01:23:45.204 --> 01:23:52.644
Eunho: I'm truly so grateful... I really couldn't have expected it...
I truly couldn't have anticipated it...

01:23:53.284 --> 01:23:59.795
Eunho: Just like the hyungs said... We only wanted PLAVE and PLLI to
be happy together...

01:23:59.835 --> 01:24:03.124
Eunho: ...and to share good music with PLLI.

01:24:09.004 --> 01:24:14.984
Eunho: I'm sorry... I don't know, it's just... We know how hard you've
worked, PLLI... I'm sorry...

01:24:16.144 --> 01:24:19.824
Yejun: You lose sleep and keep cheering us on—we know.

01:24:24.024 --> 01:24:26.964
Yejun: Thank you, truly.

01:24:29.964 --> 01:24:32.404
Noah: We'll work many times harder...

01:24:33.104 --> 01:24:38.515
Noah: ...and do our absolute best to show you even better sides of us
and even better music.

01:24:41.144 --> 01:24:47.284
Yejun: Let's create something new again, together, the five of us.
We'll create something new that PLLI will love.

01:24:50.811 --> 01:24:56.724
Yejun: Our album only came out a week ago—let's enjoy this moment! New
career high!

01:24:56.764 --> 01:24:58.164
Hamin: Let's enjoy it

01:24:59.384 --> 01:25:01.324
Yejun: Thank you.

01:25:02.364 --> 01:25:04.599
Yejun: Congratulations—let's enjoy it!

01:25:04.944 --> 01:25:07.061
Yejun: Congratulations, PLLI. Truly!

01:25:08.024 --> 01:25:13.584
Hamin: Bamby-ssi... Please say a word.
Bamby: Me? I don't know how to put this into words.

01:25:19.644 --> 01:25:24.408
Bamby: We call it receiving a gift, but what I really feel is all of
your hearts.

01:25:28.244 --> 01:25:33.234
Bamby: Like Yejun-hyung said, I do feel a little sorry—but I won't be
sorry anymore.

01:25:35.504 --> 01:25:38.454
Bamby: I want to enjoy this moment, and I hope you'll enjoy it with
us.

01:25:38.494 --> 01:25:44.023
Bamby: You all worked to create this festival atmosphere with us, so
let's celebrate together.

01:25:47.004 --> 01:25:52.121
Bamby: We'll spend the rest of today happily too. Thank you so much. I
love you, truly.

01:25:53.464 --> 01:25:55.993
Yejun: Let's enjoy too.
Eunho: Let's enjoy!

01:26:02.904 --> 01:26:04.315
Yejun: We really did it.

01:26:05.244 --> 01:26:07.844
Bamby: I mean, this is like... wow.
Yejun: Wow, this is unbelievable. Seriously.

01:26:07.884 --> 01:26:09.484
Yejun: PLLI, this is seriously amazing. Seriously.

01:26:09.524 --> 01:26:12.876
Bamby: PLLI, you're seriously incredible—this is no joke.

01:26:13.424 --> 01:26:16.264
Eunho: Wow... Seriously...
Yejun: Wow, cool.

01:26:16.304 --> 01:26:18.264
Eunho: Amazing... Seriously... How do you...
Yejun: Cool. Really cool.

01:26:18.304 --> 01:26:20.304
Hamin: I love you fiercely, truly.

01:26:21.224 --> 01:26:25.384
Noah: It wasn't that I chose not to expect it—I couldn't even imagine
it, just like HAMIN said.

01:26:25.424 --> 01:26:28.204
Yejun: Yeah. Yeah. Oh, what do I do?

01:26:29.904 --> 01:26:33.551
Yejun: Our previous album's results were already unbelievable.

01:26:35.284 --> 01:26:38.813
Bamby: What should I do? I just can't express it. Seriously.

01:26:39.284 --> 01:26:44.695
Hamin: You're telling us to enjoy it together again—how exactly are we
supposed to enjoy it?

01:26:49.404 --> 01:26:52.992
Hamin: I think we should simply enjoy this feeling right now.

01:26:53.144 --> 01:26:54.967
Yejun: I'm really, truly happy.

01:26:55.544 --> 01:26:57.904
Yejun: I feel so proud.

01:26:59.004 --> 01:27:03.121
Hamin: It feels like we're doing well.
Yejun: We made this album well.

01:27:03.244 --> 01:27:09.008
Yejun: Seeing how much PLLI love it...the performances and
everything—we did a good job making it.

01:27:13.164 --> 01:27:14.564
Eunho: I feel proud!

01:27:15.444 --> 01:27:18.738
Eunho: I feel relieved, proud, grateful—and sorry too...

01:27:20.937 --> 01:27:25.995
Eunho: PLLI tell me not to feel sorry, but I still do. So many
emotions are coming up.

01:27:29.244 --> 01:27:35.646
Hamin: Let's remember this feeling clearly. For now, let's sit down
and continue what we were doing...

01:27:38.904 --> 01:27:42.944
Hamin: ...and then close by expressing our gratitude once more.

01:27:44.984 --> 01:27:50.219
Yejun: Some PLLI are probably watching together right now.
Eunho: This is really amazing.

01:27:51.764 --> 01:27:54.646
Bamby: Earlier, I really committed to the acting.

01:27:56.604 --> 01:27:59.984
Hamin: Oh, do you wish you'd done more?
Noah: Then, Bamby, want to do it one more time?

01:28:00.024 --> 01:28:01.904
Yejun: I was just about to say that!

01:28:01.944 --> 01:28:04.044
Noah: The outfits are right on point.

01:28:04.084 --> 01:28:08.436
Bamby: No, this won't work.
Hamin: ja, let's have you do sarang-kkun once.

01:28:09.204 --> 01:28:12.524
Hamin: Give us career-high love—Bamby's sarang-kkun, please!

01:28:12.564 --> 01:28:14.224
Bamby: No—the outfit isn't ready!

01:28:14.264 --> 01:28:18.264
Yejun: No, no. I'll do it. I'll take care of it. I'll do it for you.

01:28:20.264 --> 01:28:22.764
Noah: Dudu wanted to do sarang-kkun earlier but couldn't, so he was
disappointed.

01:28:22.804 --> 01:28:28.156
Bamby: So love was waiting for me all along.
Eunho: Nice! ja, sagi-kkun! Sagi-kkun, please!

01:28:28.764 --> 01:28:30.864
Hamin: ja, sori-kkun—give us sori-kkun!

01:28:30.904 --> 01:28:33.021
Noah: ja, let's go with sarang-kkun!

01:28:33.424 --> 01:28:34.644
Bamby: I did have something prepared.

01:28:34.684 --> 01:28:37.804
Yejun: ja, Prepared or not, just feel it. Go with the moment.

01:28:37.844 --> 01:28:40.432
Hamin: Feel it—enjoy it!
Eunho: Freestyle...

01:28:42.644 --> 01:28:45.484
Eunho: Hey, you always start by jumping! [Laughs]
Bamby: First, I jump for the intro.

01:28:45.524 --> 01:28:49.053
Eunho: Sorry—I won't interrupt.
Hamin: Don't break his flow.

01:28:50.964 --> 01:28:56.104
Noah: Right—you always start by jumping. Okay, got it.
Eunho: It's his routine—he has a set routine.

01:28:56.144 --> 01:28:59.379
Yejun: At the beginning, there can be an awkward pause.

01:28:59.504 --> 01:29:04.209
Yejun: In our terms, when that dead air appears, I fill it by running
like this.

01:29:05.104 --> 01:29:06.564
Noah: I'm curious about something.

01:29:06.604 --> 01:29:09.264
Noah: Bamby, is there a reason you run in that particular pose?

01:29:09.304 --> 01:29:11.784
Yejun: Maybe because he's doing sarang-kkun? It looks cute.

01:29:11.824 --> 01:29:13.544
Bamby: Because I'm a person full of love.

01:29:13.584 --> 01:29:15.704
Eunho: And you always run as if you're in a hurry. Okay, okay.

01:29:15.744 --> 01:29:17.464
Hamin: ja, here we go. Ready!

01:29:26.064 --> 01:29:28.240
[Bamby performs a romantic freestyle]

01:29:42.484 --> 01:29:45.324
Hamin: Wait, that's the end?
Bamby: I thought there was going to be something huge.

01:29:45.364 --> 01:29:46.924
Noah: I thought so too—but it was impressive.

01:29:46.964 --> 01:29:49.524
Bamby: It was impressive—more than impressive. It was something new.
Yejun: I just went for it with momentum.

01:29:49.564 --> 01:29:51.304
Hamin: It was fresh to hear!

01:29:51.344 --> 01:29:55.844
Bamby: ja, this is great. Yes. Nice.
Noah: Nice momentum—an award for effort!

01:29:55.884 --> 01:29:57.644
Eunho: Ah... nice.
Bamby: Then.

01:29:57.684 --> 01:29:59.764
Yejun: So, anyway. Yes.

01:29:59.804 --> 01:30:05.804
Bamby: Let's move on—we still have plenty left to cover.
Hamin: Come on, Bamby-ssi—your energy is coming back now.

01:30:05.884 --> 01:30:12.304
Bamby: Great. ja, next up: analyzing the choreography for 'Starting
Race.'

01:30:14.204 --> 01:30:19.138
Bamby: ja, we've answered your questions, thanked PLLI, and even
celebrated our career high.

01:30:19.178 --> 01:30:22.825
Bamby: We also received many questions about the choreography.

01:30:24.204 --> 01:30:28.498
Bamby: To answer them, how about we show the choreography from verse
one?

01:30:30.204 --> 01:30:34.968
Bamby: If you're all okay with it, we'll go ahead and start the
choreography now.

01:30:36.164 --> 01:30:42.164
Hamin: Will we do it without music while explaining?
Bamby: Choreography doesn't come with accompaniment.

01:30:42.904 --> 01:30:45.644
Bamby: Right—'without accompaniment.' The mu means 'without.'

01:30:45.684 --> 01:30:47.584
Noah: So we're actually dancing now?
Bamby: Of course.

01:30:47.624 --> 01:30:50.944
Noah: You mean dance without music?
Hamin: We'll dance while explaining what we intended.

01:30:50.984 --> 01:30:52.964
Eunho: But why do we have to do it without music?

01:30:53.004 --> 01:30:54.904
Eunho: Can't we use the backing track and have fun with it?

01:30:54.944 --> 01:30:57.364
Hamin: Then we wouldn't be able to explain it.

01:30:57.404 --> 01:30:59.024
Bamby: We'll use music from the second run-through.

01:30:59.064 --> 01:31:04.005
Noah: If the dance line moves on without explaining something, can we
ask questions?

01:31:05.624 --> 01:31:06.824
Bamby: Of course.
Noah: Okay, I'll ask when I have one.

01:31:06.864 --> 01:31:09.904
Yejun: But right now... right now is the Dance Duo's moment, isn't it?

01:31:09.944 --> 01:31:13.684
Yejun: If the dance line says 'stop' mid-demonstration...

01:31:15.064 --> 01:31:16.744
Yejun: ...you have to freeze exactly where you are.

01:31:16.784 --> 01:31:22.784
Yejun: Yeah. You know what I mean? Let's do that.
Eunho: Don't use this as an excuse to make me exercise...

01:31:26.244 --> 01:31:28.949
Eunho: ...or deliberately make it hard for me.

01:31:29.444 --> 01:31:30.704
Hamin: ja, let's get into the opening formation.

01:31:30.744 --> 01:31:34.391
Noah: 'Don't try to make it hard for me'—why is that so funny?

01:31:35.904 --> 01:31:37.884
Hamin: The intention starts right from this opening formation.

01:31:37.924 --> 01:31:39.747
Eunho: Even this has a meaning?

01:31:40.104 --> 01:31:41.764
Noah: Right at the very beginning...

01:31:41.804 --> 01:31:43.644
Yejun: We need an overhead shot for this, don't we?

01:31:43.684 --> 01:31:46.625
Hamin: Do we have a top view?
Bamby: Oh. There is.

01:31:51.124 --> 01:31:53.124
Bamby: This RC car is really cute.

01:31:59.224 --> 01:32:02.047
Yejun: You can just stand there. Just like that.

01:32:02.204 --> 01:32:04.524
Hamin: There was a reason we chose this exact opening formation.

01:32:04.564 --> 01:32:09.564
Hamin: When creating choreography, the beginning and ending are
especially important.

01:32:13.400 --> 01:32:19.341
Hamin: If you get stuck on the opening, everything takes longer. I
thought deeply about how to begin.

01:32:19.964 --> 01:32:24.230
Hamin: I think I spent several days on this question alone.

01:32:27.364 --> 01:32:33.364
Hamin: Since it's a trace—the trail or orbit of a star—we decided to
express that through our movement paths.

01:32:33.750 --> 01:32:37.364
Hamin: Our idea was to use the PLAVE logo.

01:32:37.924 --> 01:32:43.044
Hamin: The logo has this P-shaped path, like this.

01:32:43.424 --> 01:32:46.104
Hamin: We move along that exact path.

01:32:46.944 --> 01:32:52.826
Bamby: Think of a constellation like the Big Dipper...the points
connect to create a shape.

01:32:52.866 --> 01:32:56.327
Bamby: That's the idea: each place we stand becomes a star in the
logo-shaped constellation.

01:32:56.367 --> 01:32:59.308
Bamby: Oh, the reference graphic is on screen now.

01:33:03.124 --> 01:33:05.884
Bamby: That's the way to visualize it.
Noah: So it's a constellation shaped like the PLAVE logo?

01:33:05.924 --> 01:33:10.122
Hamin: ja, exactly. We'll move along that path. Let us show you.

01:33:13.024 --> 01:33:16.464
Bamby: The path will be drawn as a trace. And the logo remains behind.

01:33:16.504 --> 01:33:19.604
Hamin: We exit by following that path.

01:33:19.644 --> 01:33:22.996
Bamby: And I come out alone for the 'I'm all alone' part.

01:33:23.124 --> 01:33:27.144
Bamby: I come out by myself.
Noah: So the choreography matches the 'I'm all alone' line?

01:33:27.184 --> 01:33:28.264
Noah: That's genius.

01:33:28.304 --> 01:33:31.884
Bamby: This hyung is always late to the realization—but he's an expert
at it.

01:33:31.924 --> 01:33:34.744
Hamin: It's been a while since we used 'late to the party.'

01:33:34.784 --> 01:33:37.284
Bamby: His late reaction makes me feel like I've been hit in the back
of the head.

01:33:37.324 --> 01:33:38.924
Noah: I knew—I was just narrating it in PLLI mode.

01:33:38.964 --> 01:33:41.004
Bamby: Oh, you were just reacting for us.

01:33:41.044 --> 01:33:43.244
Eunho: Commentary—got it.
Noah: I was giving a reaction.

01:33:43.284 --> 01:33:47.304
Yejun: Right, we need reactions. It's all pumasi.
Bamby: Good reaction!

01:33:47.344 --> 01:33:48.744
Bamby: Ah, pumasi?

01:33:49.184 --> 01:33:53.004
Bamby: ja, it all comes back to you in the end. Do good, and good
comes back to you.

01:33:53.044 --> 01:33:58.514
Hamin: Originally, Bamby-hyung was going to do the entire 'I'm all
alone' section by himself.

01:33:59.164 --> 01:34:02.222
Hamin: I had also staged the opening with him alone.

01:34:03.264 --> 01:34:07.124
Hamin: The plan was for him to keep moving alone like this...

01:34:07.584 --> 01:34:12.644
Hamin: ...but it looked too empty, so I gradually added the other
members.

01:34:13.784 --> 01:34:17.784
Bamby: The idea was: 'I'm all alone, but I don't really feel alone.'

01:34:19.264 --> 01:34:23.444
Bamby: I wanted the choreography to express being alone, yet not truly
alone.

01:34:23.484 --> 01:34:26.484
Bamby: Wait—what choreography did I do there again?

01:34:26.844 --> 01:34:30.104
Bamby: No, wait a moment...
Noah: Who are you asking?

01:34:30.144 --> 01:34:32.244
Hamin: I didn't choreograph every detail of the individual parts.

01:34:32.284 --> 01:34:34.044
Bamby: Give me a moment.

01:34:38.864 --> 01:34:41.511
Noah: What's with this guy?
Eunho: Bamby-ssi!

01:34:43.184 --> 01:34:49.744
Eunho: We just hit a career high—pull yourself together!
Bamby: Give me a moment—I'll remember and explain it.

01:34:53.664 --> 01:34:59.836
Hamin: From the next line onward, Yejun-ssi and I begin to appear.

01:35:00.304 --> 01:35:04.104
Noah: So that's why the two of you become visible?
Bamby: Ah, now I remember.

01:35:04.144 --> 01:35:06.144
Eunho: Oh, so that was coordinated?
Bamby: Nice—pumasi! I like the mutual help.

01:35:06.184 --> 01:35:09.004
Noah: Wow, so that's how the interpretation works!
Eunho: So it all lines up.

01:35:09.044 --> 01:35:10.444
Bamby: Pumasi—nice.

01:35:12.924 --> 01:35:14.629
Bamby: Pumasi makes this fun.

01:35:18.324 --> 01:35:23.384
Hamin: Bamby-ssi created this section. Should we explain its narrative
too?

01:35:23.424 --> 01:35:28.564
Bamby: Of course—though this part doesn't have any special meaning.

01:35:29.924 --> 01:35:32.884
Hamin: You probably shouldn't say it quite like that on air.
Eunho: Seriously, what's going on with you today...?

01:35:32.924 --> 01:35:34.864
Bamby: But I'm serious—no, wait...

01:35:34.904 --> 01:35:38.324
Noah: Why would you say that now?
Eunho: Hamin-ssi, do something about him!

01:35:38.364 --> 01:35:41.599
Bamby: Look, not every move can have a special meaning.

01:35:41.884 --> 01:35:44.944
Bamby: This part was simply based on the rhythm and feel.

01:35:44.984 --> 01:35:50.984
Hamin: We can always create a meaning for it now.
Bamby: You're making it up as you please. ja, from here...

01:35:52.724 --> 01:35:59.746
Hamin: The movement unfolds in sequence. A star passes by, and the
others sweep along its orbit like a trailing path.

01:36:02.224 --> 01:36:04.684
Bamby: Right—the movement leaves a trail like an orbit.

01:36:04.724 --> 01:36:09.144
Hamin: So the choreography represents the traces left by passing
planets, right?

01:36:09.184 --> 01:36:10.544
Bamby: That's exactly right.

01:36:10.584 --> 01:36:16.964
Hamin: So that really was the intention. Shall we demonstrate it?

01:36:17.084 --> 01:36:19.664
Bamby: [Quotes the English lyric]

01:36:20.304 --> 01:36:22.144
Bamby: Everyone except HAMIN becomes one of the stars...

01:36:22.184 --> 01:36:23.864
Noah: So all of the stars are flying away?
Yejun: Right, they're flying away.

01:36:23.904 --> 01:36:26.064
Hamin: The constellation follows along behind.

01:36:26.104 --> 01:36:28.124
Bamby: The stars stream past.

01:36:28.444 --> 01:36:33.914
Bamby: The intention here was this: when the camera catches me in a
bust shot as I pass by...

01:36:34.382 --> 01:36:39.029
Bamby: ...the members rise one by one, appearing like a trail I've
left behind.

01:36:42.484 --> 01:36:48.144
Hamin: Like silhouettes appearing behind you.
Bamby: Right, one by one... what was the move again?

01:36:48.184 --> 01:36:50.125
Bamby: You sweep your arm upward.

01:36:51.504 --> 01:36:52.584
Noah: Don't we all rise the same way?
Yejun: We do rise the same way.

01:36:52.624 --> 01:36:55.859
Bamby: It's the timing that makes it happen one by one.

01:36:57.144 --> 01:37:00.379
Bamby: As I pass, they become the trail I leave behind.

01:37:01.524 --> 01:37:05.044
Bamby: Imagine the camera has me in a bust shot here.

01:37:05.944 --> 01:37:08.784
Bamby: As soon as the shot lands on me, the members appear one by
one—bam, bam, bam.

01:37:08.824 --> 01:37:10.584
Hamin: Almost like they're recalling you.

01:37:10.624 --> 01:37:12.624
Bamby: Then we gather and lift together here.

01:37:12.664 --> 01:37:14.864
Hamin: There's another detail here we almost missed...

01:37:14.904 --> 01:37:16.304
Bamby: Where?

01:37:19.684 --> 01:37:22.154
Hamin: The part about the opposite side...

01:37:22.504 --> 01:37:26.084
Eunho: [Quotes the English lyric]

01:37:28.884 --> 01:37:32.204
Hamin: Right—the other side, a different space.
Bamby: We move toward the other side there.

01:37:32.244 --> 01:37:34.864
Eunho: There is a meaning here, right? Okay, good.
Hamin: There is—you almost missed this detail.

01:37:34.904 --> 01:37:39.256
Bamby: The others deliberately face that direction, while I face this
way.

01:37:40.461 --> 01:37:44.504
Bamby: I step backward, then turn to face the opposite side.

01:37:47.658 --> 01:37:50.604
Bamby: That was intentional too.
Hamin: So there's another world on the opposite side.

01:37:50.644 --> 01:37:55.704
Bamby: Right—and here I break through that world.

01:38:03.124 --> 01:38:05.888
Bamby: That's where the story begins to unfold.

01:38:09.244 --> 01:38:11.324
Hamin: Shall we demonstrate this section?

01:38:11.364 --> 01:38:16.087
Hamin: [Demonstrates the choreography to the song]

01:38:20.164 --> 01:38:25.222
Hamin: Up to this point, I think this came from the original
choreography draft video.

01:38:25.724 --> 01:38:30.284
Hamin: I really liked it. The footwork here was slightly different in
the draft...

01:38:30.324 --> 01:38:32.735
Eunho: I have a question about this part.

01:38:35.000 --> 01:38:39.588
Eunho: Why did you tell us to hit 'boom' and hold the move only to
this point?

01:38:40.384 --> 01:38:44.684
Hamin: You're not simply holding it there...you carry that 'boom'
through until your own part.

01:38:44.724 --> 01:38:47.884
Eunho: Was there a reason you told us not to lower it all the way
here?

01:38:47.924 --> 01:38:51.344
Hamin: If you drop all the way on 'boom,' there's nothing left for the
next movement.

01:38:51.384 --> 01:38:53.384
Hamin: Right—it leaves a lingering aftereffect.
Noah: This is synchronized group choreography.

01:38:53.424 --> 01:38:55.804
Eunho: Ah, so it's a choreographic detail.

01:38:55.844 --> 01:39:01.364
Hamin: Each member completes the movement when their own part arrives.

01:39:02.744 --> 01:39:04.324
Hamin: [Demonstrates the next movement]

01:39:04.364 --> 01:39:06.364
Noah: What determines the order we enter here?

01:39:06.404 --> 01:39:08.624
Eunho: Does that order have a meaning?

01:39:08.664 --> 01:39:10.304
Hamin: I'm moving around as if searching for what I need.

01:39:10.344 --> 01:39:12.144
Noah: Oh, that's what it means. Got it.

01:39:12.184 --> 01:39:15.084
Yejun: It's almost like a star's journey.
Hamin: It's definitely a journey.

01:39:15.124 --> 01:39:16.524
Bamby: Star travel.

01:39:18.044 --> 01:39:21.396
Hamin: As I move like this, my gaze follows the motion...

01:39:23.224 --> 01:39:26.304
Hamin: ...so I experience the moment alone through my eyeline.

01:39:26.344 --> 01:39:29.226
Eunho: So it even accounts for performing live...

01:39:30.204 --> 01:39:33.024
Hamin: Then, at the next line...

01:39:34.144 --> 01:39:37.064
Hamin: The movement spreads outward here...

01:39:37.104 --> 01:39:39.024
Eunho: ...then—bam!

01:39:39.064 --> 01:39:42.464
Hamin: Bam! I smash through this wall.

01:39:44.404 --> 01:39:47.462
Bamby: This next move came to us almost immediately.

01:39:48.824 --> 01:39:54.118
Hamin: Right. It started from matching the sound, but the move also
had a clear intention.

01:39:55.364 --> 01:40:01.104
Hamin: It had impact—the idea was to break through a wall...but the
wall doesn't actually break at first.

01:40:01.144 --> 01:40:03.064
Bamby: Oh no—it still hasn't broken through?

01:40:03.104 --> 01:40:06.224
Hamin: Bang, bang—it doesn't break. Then you fasten your seat belt and
set off.

01:40:06.264 --> 01:40:07.664
Yejun: A seat belt?

01:40:09.664 --> 01:40:11.524
Hamin: Right—you fasten it and start the race immediately.

01:40:11.564 --> 01:40:15.624
Eunho: But Bamby-ssi, I don't hit it like this—I use this instead.

01:40:15.664 --> 01:40:18.724
Bamby: You're bringing that up again.
Eunho: Is this supposed to be an energy blast or what?

01:40:18.764 --> 01:40:23.884
Eunho: I mean, you go like this—boom, boom—twice. Wasn't the original
move meant to hit the other members?

01:40:23.924 --> 01:40:27.144
Hamin: It's your own personal wall—you are trying to break through it.

01:40:27.184 --> 01:40:29.504
Yejun: Ah, there is our shared wall, but each person has their own
wall too.

01:40:29.544 --> 01:40:33.204
Eunho: Then why don't you strike it with your elbow? Why use an energy
blast like this?

01:40:33.244 --> 01:40:35.704
Bamby: I did use my elbow at first.
Hamin: That actually suits you way better.

01:40:35.744 --> 01:40:37.064
Bamby: That's the style—the flair.

01:40:37.104 --> 01:40:40.986
Eunho: After the strike... I thought he was doing an energy blast.

01:40:41.824 --> 01:40:43.624
Hamin: Eunho would strike it like this—not like this.

01:40:43.664 --> 01:40:46.124
Eunho: Oh! So that's why this move was added? I finally understand.

01:40:46.164 --> 01:40:48.987
Hamin: I consider every detail when I create it.

01:40:53.084 --> 01:40:56.025
Hamin: [Demonstrates the choreography to the song]

01:41:04.444 --> 01:41:06.855
Bamby: This section combined a few ideas.

01:41:08.504 --> 01:41:11.084
Bamby: And Eunho's move here was created entirely from scratch.

01:41:11.124 --> 01:41:13.653
Hamin: Right—Bamby-hyung created this part.

01:41:14.704 --> 01:41:19.904
Bamby: When I first heard the music, I pictured something different
for this part.

01:41:20.064 --> 01:41:26.064
Bamby: Normally, you might expect everyone to perform the same
synchronized choreography in the chorus.

01:41:27.508 --> 01:41:30.978
Bamby: But I didn't want the first chorus to work that way.

01:41:31.584 --> 01:41:37.525
Bamby: I thought it would feel fresher if the member singing the
chorus did something striking alone.

01:41:40.144 --> 01:41:45.944
Bamby: Let us show it once. Eunho-ssi sharply turns the steering wheel
here.

01:41:46.104 --> 01:41:48.044
Bamby: That sends the rest of us swerving the other way.

01:41:48.084 --> 01:41:51.907
Yejun: To add one more detail: the music itself keeps developing.

01:41:54.044 --> 01:41:56.524
Yejun: The first verse is not as intense yet.

01:41:56.564 --> 01:42:01.164
Bamby: Right—the first verse lacks the drums that appear in verse two.
Yejun: It keeps building and building.

01:42:01.204 --> 01:42:05.026
Bamby: So the two choruses could not use identical choreography. When
Eunho sends us swerving...

01:42:05.066 --> 01:42:08.424
Bamby: ...we recoil, and then he drops out of the formation.

01:42:08.464 --> 01:42:10.884
Noah: Ah, so the car sends everyone flying aside?

01:42:10.924 --> 01:42:15.644
Yejun: So in the first verse, the racers are still in the middle of
their journey.

01:42:15.684 --> 01:42:18.084
Hamin: They are still unpolished racers.

01:42:19.364 --> 01:42:22.204
Hamin: [Demonstrates the next racing movement]

01:42:23.004 --> 01:42:26.704
Hamin: This also came from the draft, but we developed it further.

01:42:26.744 --> 01:42:29.504
Bamby: We changed this part extensively.

01:42:29.624 --> 01:42:31.704
Hamin: This section was difficult to work out.

01:42:31.744 --> 01:42:33.364
Bamby: [Quotes the English lyric]

01:42:33.404 --> 01:42:39.584
Hamin: [Demonstrates the difficult movement sequence]

01:42:40.024 --> 01:42:42.264
Hamin: We draw the trail of a star...

01:42:42.804 --> 01:42:45.451
Hamin: ...leaving that trace along its orbit.

01:42:47.444 --> 01:42:50.144
Hamin: [Marks the beat while demonstrating]

01:42:50.584 --> 01:42:54.904
Hamin: We leave another trail here, and then enter the dance break.

01:42:56.764 --> 01:43:00.324
Hamin: This section was choreographed mainly to match the sound.

01:43:00.364 --> 01:43:04.024
Noah: So this is pure sound-driven choreography, without a lyrical
meaning.

01:43:04.064 --> 01:43:06.864
Bamby: There is still a subtle concept here.

01:43:07.164 --> 01:43:10.987
Bamby: In the later part, when everyone gathers in slow motion...

01:43:13.184 --> 01:43:18.301
Hamin: Is this the gravity concept?
Bamby: Right—zero gravity and a mechanical quality.

01:43:18.345 --> 01:43:21.286
Bamby: That led to these stiff, precise movements.

01:43:22.944 --> 01:43:24.944
Hamin: It feels almost mechanical.

01:43:25.304 --> 01:43:26.904
Noah: Almost like a doll or toy.

01:43:26.944 --> 01:43:31.331
Bamby: [Demonstrates the mechanical movement] The machine glitches for
a moment...

01:43:31.371 --> 01:43:34.959
Bamby: ...becomes weightless, then snaps back into alignment.

01:43:36.984 --> 01:43:41.224
Hamin: Exactly—like a broken toy suddenly repairing itself.

01:43:41.264 --> 01:43:46.734
Yejun: I move smoothly here, then suddenly rotate like this. That made
it feel robotic to me.

01:43:50.044 --> 01:43:53.564
Hamin: It shows the racers becoming fully refined as verse two
approaches.

01:43:53.604 --> 01:43:55.780
Eunho: There is a lot of detail here.

01:43:55.944 --> 01:43:57.464
Eunho: Wow, that's amazing.

01:43:57.504 --> 01:44:00.124
Bamby: Did you think we were just winging it without any details?

01:44:00.164 --> 01:44:05.869
Eunho: Did you really have to put it that way?
Hamin: [Demonstrates the choreography to the song]

01:44:09.044 --> 01:44:10.664
Bamby: ja, let us move to the next section.

01:44:10.704 --> 01:44:14.364
Bamby: [Demonstrates the next lyric and movement]

01:44:15.544 --> 01:44:17.544
Hamin: The moment I heard this part, I said we absolutely had to
include this move.

01:44:17.584 --> 01:44:22.344
Bamby: Right—Hamin said that at the time. Here is another
behind-the-scenes story.

01:44:22.384 --> 01:44:27.264
Bamby: This time, we taught the choreography to five dancers...

01:44:29.744 --> 01:44:33.449
Bamby: ...so each dancer could then coach one of us one-on-one.

01:44:36.224 --> 01:44:41.165
Bamby: We needed dancers who could help each member with movement
paths and details.

01:44:45.969 --> 01:44:49.144
Bamby: While we were teaching, Hamin kept suggesting extra details.

01:44:49.184 --> 01:44:53.125
Bamby: He would say, 'Hyung, I think we should add something here.'

01:44:55.444 --> 01:44:57.684
Bamby: Then he said, 'We should choreograph this part quickly.'

01:44:57.724 --> 01:44:59.371
Hamin: Are you imitating me?

01:45:00.323 --> 01:45:03.734
Bamby: So I took that idea and choreographed this section.

01:45:04.124 --> 01:45:05.844
Hamin: Do you remember that?
Bamby: I remember that behind-the-scenes moment.

01:45:05.884 --> 01:45:07.884
Hamin: Ah, that was the moment you meant.
Bamby: Yes, exactly.

01:45:07.924 --> 01:45:11.335
Hamin: This came to me the moment I heard the guide track.

01:45:13.604 --> 01:45:18.427
Hamin: It was Noah-hyung's part, and his voice has this unmistakably
sexy quality.

01:45:20.401 --> 01:45:23.604
Hamin: [Demonstrates the movement dynamics]

01:45:25.444 --> 01:45:29.796
Hamin: The movement needed a clear contrast between strength and
softness.

01:45:30.204 --> 01:45:35.684
Hamin: Exactly. It begins heavy, releases into a wave, then evokes a
falling star.

01:45:36.644 --> 01:45:39.644
Hamin: [Demonstrates the next sequence to the song]

01:45:50.744 --> 01:45:53.567
Hamin: We continue through the next movements...

01:45:55.364 --> 01:45:58.305
Hamin: This hand sign evokes Formula 1 and racing.

01:46:02.524 --> 01:46:07.876
Hamin: Here, the two racers are on different teams, but we imagined
them showing fair play.

01:46:12.004 --> 01:46:16.533
Hamin: They are opposing teams, but this face-off still represents
fair play.

01:46:21.244 --> 01:46:26.164
Bamby: So that is another meaning behind the hand sign. Because racing
is also about fair play. It all fits together.

01:46:26.204 --> 01:46:30.674
Hamin: We changed the movement paths considerably to make this pairing
work.

01:46:32.164 --> 01:46:37.444
Hamin: We continue through this part, then move into the chorus.

01:46:38.524 --> 01:46:40.884
Hamin: [References the next lyric and movement]

01:46:40.924 --> 01:46:43.244
Yejun: The force stays consistent here.
Bamby: Ah, this is where they glare at each other.

01:46:43.284 --> 01:46:45.904
Hamin: Bamby-hyung and I are on opposing teams here.

01:46:45.944 --> 01:46:48.564
Noah: Ah, so that is why the two of you glare at each other?
Hamin: Right—we are confronting each other as rivals.

01:46:48.604 --> 01:46:51.864
Hamin: [Demonstrates the rival-facing movement to the song]

01:46:51.904 --> 01:46:54.964
Hamin: This is the moment just before the racers take their starting
positions.

01:46:55.004 --> 01:46:59.062
Hamin: Here we jump, raise the trophy, then draw it toward the heart.

01:47:09.364 --> 01:47:13.658
Hamin: I drew inspiration from the music video, where I throw the
helmet.

01:47:15.444 --> 01:47:19.385
Hamin: I thought that image could translate well into choreography.

01:47:19.904 --> 01:47:23.184
Bamby: Oh, so that movement came from throwing the helmet.

01:47:23.224 --> 01:47:24.944
Noah: So the choreography represents throwing the helmet?

01:47:24.984 --> 01:47:29.572
Hamin: It does not literally depict the throw—I only took inspiration
from it.

01:47:30.204 --> 01:47:34.086
Bamby: I also want to explain the fine-grained meaning in my part.

01:47:39.344 --> 01:47:41.084
Bamby: I raise the trophy...

01:47:43.324 --> 01:47:47.924
Bamby: ...bring it into my chest, curve around...
Yejun: Bringing it to the heart.

01:47:47.964 --> 01:47:51.344
Bamby: ...and place my bet on you. That was the idea.

01:47:52.884 --> 01:47:55.344
Bamby: All packed into a tiny detail.
Noah: So you gave the move different meanings?

01:47:55.384 --> 01:47:57.104
Bamby: The meaning is the same.

01:47:57.144 --> 01:47:59.624
Noah: Ah, because Bamby is in the center.

01:48:03.224 --> 01:48:06.106
Bamby: [Continues the choreography demonstration]

01:48:07.904 --> 01:48:12.021
Hamin: This next part came from an external choreography team's draft.

01:48:14.004 --> 01:48:19.356
Hamin: [Demonstrates the transition] The second verse and chorus
remain the same from here.

01:48:24.624 --> 01:48:29.388
Yejun: Shall we move to the dance break?
Hamin: ja, let us go to the dance break.

01:48:32.004 --> 01:48:33.664
Hamin: [Demonstrates the dance-break beat]

01:48:33.704 --> 01:48:38.233
Eunho: Before that, PLLI were curious about the part where I am pulled
along.

01:48:39.064 --> 01:48:40.704
Hamin: What is the meaning of this part?

01:48:40.744 --> 01:48:43.224
Noah: What was the reason behind it?
Eunho: I have no idea.

01:48:43.264 --> 01:48:47.444
Bamby: It is telling an agitated Eunho to calm down.

01:48:48.184 --> 01:48:51.564
Noah: So the choreography is calming down a shouting Eunho?

01:48:51.604 --> 01:48:57.133
Hamin: For me, the image came from the sound and its buildup just
before the dance break hits.

01:48:59.644 --> 01:49:03.761
Hamin: I wanted an urgent, desperate performance image at that moment.

01:49:04.084 --> 01:49:06.584
Yejun: So the key emotion is desperation.

01:49:07.684 --> 01:49:10.524
Hamin: [Demonstrates the escalating movement]

01:49:12.124 --> 01:49:18.124
Bamby: What looked so cool was Hamin entering calmly and dancing while
everyone else was being dragged along in a frenzy.

01:49:19.806 --> 01:49:22.004
Bamby: It felt like Hamin was saying, 'You stay back.'

01:49:22.044 --> 01:49:26.444
Bamby: 'I will handle this.' That confidence made the entrance look so
cool.

01:49:26.484 --> 01:49:30.584
Eunho: So the feeling was, 'You stay out—I will show you how it is
done.'

01:49:30.624 --> 01:49:34.004
Hamin: That is close, though my intention was slightly different.

01:49:34.044 --> 01:49:37.102
Hamin: In any case, that is the 'calm down' section.

01:49:37.784 --> 01:49:42.061
Bamby: The choreography team posted their version, and it looked
incredible. You all saw it, right?

01:49:42.101 --> 01:49:48.101
Bamby: The original choreography was excellent, but some details were
difficult for us to express naturally.

01:49:52.294 --> 01:49:56.529
Bamby: We mixed in clearer body lines and adjusted the dance to suit
us.

01:49:58.564 --> 01:50:04.564
Hamin: With five members, we needed stronger impact, tighter cohesion,
and clearly visible body lines.

01:50:06.044 --> 01:50:09.564
Hamin: We adjusted the sections where the members' power needed to
come through more clearly.

01:50:09.604 --> 01:50:14.368
Hamin: PLLI also said this bang-bang-bang motion resembles a racing
start signal.

01:50:16.504 --> 01:50:18.904
Noah: Was that meaning part of the original choreography?

01:50:18.944 --> 01:50:21.524
Hamin: The movement itself came from the original draft.
Noah: Oh, the draft already had that move?

01:50:21.564 --> 01:50:24.424
Hamin: ja, I liked the draft move so much that I interpreted it as a
start signal.

01:50:24.464 --> 01:50:27.581
Bamby: Wow, the start-signal interpretation is great.

01:50:27.724 --> 01:50:31.371
Eunho: PLLI are amazing.
Yejun: That is a cool interpretation.

01:50:36.324 --> 01:50:40.004
Hamin: We keep moving forward, then sharply shift gears.

01:50:40.964 --> 01:50:43.199
Hamin: And then the racer accelerates.

01:50:45.304 --> 01:50:51.304
Hamin: This section is less about narrative interpretation and more
about fitting the dancers and the music.

01:50:51.644 --> 01:50:56.761
Hamin: Many people were curious about this next section, which was
difficult to create.

01:50:57.944 --> 01:51:02.767
Noah: Watching Hamin and Bamby perform the draft, I thought, 'How can
we do that?'

01:51:16.704 --> 01:51:22.704
Hamin: I chose this movement because it felt like racing: someone
wins, someone loses, and the motion resembles a speedometer.

01:51:28.204 --> 01:51:31.964
Hamin: The image fits the racing concept perfectly.

01:51:35.124 --> 01:51:40.594
Bamby: I remember Hamin refining this movement extensively before
teaching it to the dancers.

01:51:41.664 --> 01:51:44.804
Bamby: I will never forget the dancers' expressions when they first
saw it.

01:51:44.844 --> 01:51:47.664
Eunho: You just switched from polite speech to casual speech—please
choose one.

01:51:47.704 --> 01:51:49.904
Bamby: What?
Eunho: Never mind—please continue.

01:51:49.944 --> 01:51:52.296
Bamby: You suddenly start nitpicking me.

01:51:52.704 --> 01:51:57.030
Bamby: Even the dancers initially reacted, 'How are we supposed to do
this?'

01:51:57.070 --> 01:52:00.364
Bamby: They mastered it in the end, but that shows how difficult the
move really was.

01:52:00.404 --> 01:52:03.564
Noah: Once you learn it, you can do it—but beforehand it feels impossible.
Eunho: It was harder than I expected.

01:52:03.604 --> 01:52:07.124
Yejun: You have to perform it without consciously thinking through
every step.

01:52:07.164 --> 01:52:10.024
Bamby: Before that happens, it feels too daunting to attempt.

01:52:10.064 --> 01:52:12.304
Eunho: It takes a long time for the body to get used to it.

01:52:12.344 --> 01:52:16.407
Hamin: That is why I taught you this early on—I knew we would
definitely use it.

01:52:16.447 --> 01:52:19.664
Yejun: We learned this move before the rest of the choreography.

01:52:19.704 --> 01:52:22.351
Hamin: [They demonstrate the practice counts]

01:52:32.184 --> 01:52:37.007
Hamin: This part took a lot of work, but now the movement comes out
automatically.

01:52:41.464 --> 01:52:47.464
Noah: Do you know what happens by the end? You start with the proper
moves, then eventually think, 'Whatever!'

01:52:49.844 --> 01:52:55.224
Noah: [Laughs and demonstrates the improvised version]
Hamin: The funny thing is, viewers cannot tell.

01:52:55.264 --> 01:52:57.204
Hamin: That is what makes the choreography look so impressive.

01:52:57.244 --> 01:53:00.126
Hamin: [Continues the choreography demonstration]

01:53:05.044 --> 01:53:07.396
Hamin: The movement passes through here.

01:53:09.104 --> 01:53:11.124
Bamby: This area originally looked a little empty.

01:53:11.164 --> 01:53:15.139
Hamin: We worked hard to preserve the strongest ideas while filling
the empty spaces.

01:53:15.179 --> 01:53:18.524
Hamin: [Demonstrates the transition into the ending]

01:53:23.784 --> 01:53:29.004
Eunho: [Demonstrates the trophy movement]

01:53:29.264 --> 01:53:32.044
Bamby: This gesture represents the trophy.
Hamin: Who choreographed this section?

01:53:32.084 --> 01:53:36.084
Bamby: I think we mixed this with part of the external team's draft.

01:53:40.304 --> 01:53:44.364
Eunho: Does this part not feel like Bamby-hyung's choreography? It has
a strong Bamby-hyung feel.

01:53:44.404 --> 01:53:47.484
Noah: Most of the later choreography felt very Bamby-like to me.

01:53:47.524 --> 01:53:50.604
Hamin: Right, so Bamby-hyung probably suggested this move.

01:53:50.644 --> 01:53:51.744
Bamby: Probably, yes.

01:53:51.784 --> 01:53:55.824
Eunho: Please answer with confidence instead of saying 'probably.'

01:53:56.824 --> 01:53:59.824
Hamin: ja, that brings us to the final ending pose.

01:54:02.564 --> 01:54:08.328
Hamin: Since the song follows the traces of stars, the Big Bang image
came to mind for the ending.

01:54:11.424 --> 01:54:13.584
Hamin: The movement bursts outward like the Big Bang.

01:54:13.624 --> 01:54:18.044
Hamin: This is also an unusual, memorable ending move.

01:54:20.464 --> 01:54:25.993
Bamby: It recalls 'The 6th Summer.'
Hamin: Right—it feels like a continuation of that imagery.

01:54:26.604 --> 01:54:29.884
Yejun: Which summer are we on now?

01:54:30.004 --> 01:54:33.004
Bamby: It is not actually summer—what are we doing?

01:54:33.684 --> 01:54:38.742
Hamin: So the story progresses from a constellation's stars to the
explosive Big Bang.

01:54:42.904 --> 01:54:45.558
Hamin: It was difficult to explain while demonstrating it live.
Yejun: You did a great job.

01:54:45.598 --> 01:54:48.224
Hamin: If we find another useful interpretation later, we will share
it with you.

01:54:48.264 --> 01:54:52.264
Eunho: No, your explanation was more than enough.
Noah: It was good.

01:54:54.424 --> 01:55:00.424
Hamin: You said this choreography feels less exhausting than 'Born
Savage,' but its challenge is different.

01:55:06.104 --> 01:55:12.104
Hamin: Rather than a stamina battle, it demands many precise skills,
details, subdivisions, and tempo changes.

01:55:14.364 --> 01:55:19.422
Hamin: I think viewers will enjoy its appeal as something distinct
from 'Born Savage.'

01:55:23.024 --> 01:55:25.304
Yejun: Great work, everyone.

01:55:26.544 --> 01:55:29.904
Bamby: We have naturally ended up standing in our racing teams.

01:55:29.944 --> 01:55:35.444
Bamby: Eunho-ssi, please come forward.
Yejun: That makes me curious—who actually won the race?

01:55:35.484 --> 01:55:38.044
Yejun: Did our team win, or did yours?

01:55:38.084 --> 01:55:41.613
Eunho: Our team won.
Bamby: Oh, you mean in the music video?

01:55:41.884 --> 01:55:45.589
Bamby: At the finish line, were the two cars Bamby and Hamin's?

01:55:49.444 --> 01:55:51.244
Hamin: Mine was one of them.
Eunho: It was me.

01:55:51.284 --> 01:55:52.804
Bamby: Oh, Eunho?
Yejun: It was probably Eunho.

01:55:52.844 --> 01:55:55.404
Eunho: How can you not know that?

01:56:00.164 --> 01:56:05.222
Eunho: I know. I should know that, right, hyung?
Bamby: The shot used some CG, though.

01:56:06.684 --> 01:56:08.804
Hamin: Everything moved so fast that I barely remember it.

01:56:08.844 --> 01:56:14.844
Yejun: Honestly, when I watched the music video, Eunho's car looked
slightly closer to the finish line.

01:56:16.844 --> 01:56:18.344
Eunho: Of course it did.

01:56:18.904 --> 01:56:22.124
Yejun: But the result is still uncertain.
Hamin: The camera angle affected how it looked.

01:56:22.164 --> 01:56:25.105
Bamby: The camera creates an optical illusion too.

01:56:34.564 --> 01:56:37.864
Hamin: ja, in any case, let us leave the result as an open ending.

01:56:37.904 --> 01:56:43.668
Bamby: ja, we have shared wonderful, happy news and spent a truly fun
and meaningful day together.

01:56:50.544 --> 01:56:53.661
Bamby: ja, we will wrap up with a capture-time photo.

01:56:57.304 --> 01:56:59.424
Bamby: Get ready for capture time.

01:57:04.284 --> 01:57:06.989
Yejun: Shall we gather together for the photo?

01:57:13.684 --> 01:57:18.344
Hamin: I am at the very back.
Yejun: Wait, should we arrange this in the opposite order?

01:57:18.384 --> 01:57:19.864
Yejun: This way? Okay.

01:57:22.244 --> 01:57:24.404
Eunho: PLLI really like this pose.

01:57:40.684 --> 01:57:43.904
Yejun: Shall we take a pretty selfie too?
Hamin: Shall we give it a pretty, career-high vibe?

01:57:43.944 --> 01:57:45.649
Noah: Okay—a high-waist vibe!

01:57:52.944 --> 01:57:55.324
Yejun: Thank you, PLLI.

01:57:59.824 --> 01:58:01.824
Noah: It is hot—shall we take off our jackets?
Hamin: Shall we?

01:58:01.864 --> 01:58:04.884
Noah: One, two, three! Okay, let us go!

01:58:06.764 --> 01:58:08.411
Yejun: This is embarrassing.

01:58:17.104 --> 01:58:20.986
Bamby: The photo felt like a triumphant shot after winning a race.

01:58:23.744 --> 01:58:25.984
Hamin: What? Were you prepared for that?

01:58:26.024 --> 01:58:27.906
Eunho: Did you even rehearse it?

01:58:29.884 --> 01:58:33.648
Bamby: ja, let us take your recommendations for the ending song.

01:58:34.384 --> 01:58:38.266
Noah: Ah, malmo—'it goes without saying!'
Bamby: Balmok? 'Ankles'?

01:58:39.184 --> 01:58:42.324
Noah: Malmo!
Bamby: Is there a song called 'Balmok'?

01:58:42.764 --> 01:58:46.864
Noah: You do not know what malmo means?
Bamby: It means 'malhae mwohae'—'it goes without saying.'

01:58:46.904 --> 01:58:51.139
Noah: Malmo, malmo!
Bamby: ja, malmo—then we know exactly what you want.

01:58:51.584 --> 01:58:54.524
Bamby: Please play 'Starting Race.'

01:58:55.104 --> 01:58:56.633
Hamin: Three, two, one—go!

01:58:58.264 --> 01:59:00.264
Bamby: Are we performing the choreography too?
Noah: Of course—we have to!

01:59:00.304 --> 01:59:01.884
Yejun: Shall we? Okay.

01:59:02.004 --> 01:59:04.298
Eunho: We were just testing the waters.

01:59:06.964 --> 01:59:10.184
Noah: ja, as you watch the choreography again, keep the meanings we
just explained in mind.

01:59:10.224 --> 01:59:15.165
Bamby: Are we going full energy? Let us go full energy.
Noah: Keep it moderate—okay!

01:59:22.004 --> 01:59:25.424
Bamby: [Bamby sings in English]

01:59:30.044 --> 01:59:31.444
Yejun: [Singing]

01:59:53.044 --> 01:59:55.279
Bamby: Can we do it from farther away?

01:59:55.744 --> 01:59:57.861
Hamin: Farther away?
Bamby: Farther.

01:59:59.004 --> 02:00:00.709
Bamby: A little farther away.

02:00:00.764 --> 02:00:02.164
Bamby: Yes, perfect.

02:00:09.304 --> 02:00:10.984
Noah: Stop making me laugh!

02:00:27.184 --> 02:00:28.584
Noah: Hey—thank you!

02:00:57.004 --> 02:00:59.062
Eunho: Should I belt it out or not?

02:00:59.104 --> 02:01:00.504
Hamin: Let us hear it.

02:01:01.184 --> 02:01:05.478
Hamin: Is your throat okay right now?
Eunho: I do not know—I have to try!

02:01:05.884 --> 02:01:07.284
Hamin: Let us go!

02:01:29.364 --> 02:01:31.624
Eunho: [Eunho sings in English]

02:01:35.024 --> 02:01:37.584
Eunho: [Eunho sings in English]

02:01:53.724 --> 02:01:55.124
Hamin: Thank you!

02:01:59.104 --> 02:02:01.162
Hamin: I love you!
Yejun: Love you!
